# arm64: original memory driver, linked to PR150 7d9fc50439cd479b81872dec5ced14da121a837e.
# RSS/VSZ reads are unavailable on this OS: zero fields are NOT measurements.
# Only requested-allocation bytes are evidence; excludes allocator overhead and residency.
# Driver SHA256: 5978984fb638fc2b791d3e86f663fe03f1a77473339a3d94cff01e5b01ddc373

$ packed_mem_bench 100 10
=============================================================
 PACKED vs DENSE memory microbench (HdrHistogram_c)
=============================================================
config:  low=1 high=3600000000 sigfig=3
         counts_len=23552  -> dense per-histo committed=188520 B (184.10 KB)
workload: N=100 histograms, D=10 distinct values each (d_populatable=10)

DENSE committed (N * hdr_get_memory_size) :       18852000 B  (17.98 MB)  <- hard VSZ floor
  measured VSZ delta (address space)      :              0 B  (0.00 B)
DENSE resident  (measured RSS delta)      :              0 B  (0.00 B)  <- allocator-dependent
   -> resident is 0.0% of committed. NOTE: resident fraction is a glibc
      artifact (calloc from heap memsets -> fully resident; fresh mmap stays
      lazy). Under real many-histogram churn it trends toward 100%. The VSZ
      floor above is the unconditional cost packed eliminates.

PACKED modelled per-histo (D_pop=10, +ctx=64B, min_phys=128B):
   optimistic  (2B/entry, tight)                per= 192.00 B tot= 18.75 KB  (0.1% of committed, 0% of resident)
   realistic   (8B/entry, 1 long/entry + tree)  per= 192.00 B tot= 18.75 KB  (0.1% of committed, 0% of resident)
   pessimistic (16B/entry, tree-heavy)          per= 320.00 B tot= 31.25 KB  (0.2% of committed, 0% of resident)

MEASURED packed (Phase-2: shared geom + 1B counts, 10 populated/histo):
   exact bytes held (shared config once + N * per-histo) : 14.16 KB
   measured RSS delta (allocator incl. overhead)         : 0.00 B

verdict (measured packed exact vs dense):
   packed=14.16 KB  vs  dense committed=17.98 MB  -> 1299.8x smaller (VSZ floor)

